cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use PortPy or the PortPy.AI benchmark in your research, please cite the
  NeurIPS 2026 paper below (preferred-citation). If you use the benchmark dataset,
  please also cite the TCIA source collections listed in the README.
type: software
title: "PortPy: Planning and Optimization for Radiation Therapy in Python"
abstract: >-
  Open-source Python platform for radiotherapy treatment-planning research:
  benchmark patient data, optimization algorithms (IMRT, VMAT, mixed-integer
  references), AI-based dose prediction, and clinical plan evaluation.
